   $q$Which sentence would best open the report, before sentence 1, by making a general observation that leads into the topic?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Sewing machines were invented a long time ago.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-focus-intro"},{"text":"My grandmother has a quilt that is blue and green.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"personal-detail-intro"},{"text":"Many homes have a quilt folded on a bed, but few people know the history it holds.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Quilts are a kind of blanket.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repeats-definition"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Many homes have a quilt folded on a bed, but few people know the history it holds.$q$, $q$This sentence starts with something familiar to many readers and then points toward the report's focus, the history and meaning of quilts. "Quilts are a kind of blanket" only repeats what sentence 1 already says.$q$, 'draft', '26e5d508-9652-5d00-ba54-e21a6c7ad793')
