   $q$Sentence 8 tells the reader how the narrator feels. Which revision best shows the feeling instead?$q$, $q$[{"text":"I felt very bored about the eclipse.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"still-telling"},{"text":"I tapped my foot and sighed. \"Is that all?\" I asked.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Grandpa felt excited about the eclipse.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"changes-character-focus"},{"text":"Everyone in the world thought eclipses were boring.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralizes"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$I tapped my foot and sighed. "Is that all?" I asked.$q$, $q$Tapping a foot, sighing, and asking "Is that all?" let the reader see the boredom through actions and dialogue. "I felt very bored" still simply tells the feeling.$q$, 'draft', '7f47078a-3e1b-5a9a-b377-48ed0abd9c51')
