        '3-5', $q$Racing to the Sea$q$, $q$(1) On certain warm beaches, something amazing happens on summer nights. (2) Tiny loggerhead sea turtles dig their way out of nests buried in the sand. (3) ____, they must find their way to the ocean. (4) Scientists think the hatchlings move toward the brightest horizon, which is usually the moonlit water. (5) Bright lights from houses and streets can confuse them, however. (6) ____, some hatchlings crawl toward roads instead of the sea.

(7) Many beach towns now work to help the young turtles. (8) Some towns ask people to turn off outdoor lights during nesting season. (9) Others use special amber lights that turtles do not notice as much. (10) Volunteers also mark nests with stakes and tape so that no one steps on them. (11) Loggerheads are named for their large heads. (12) Thanks to these efforts, more hatchlings can reach the waves safely.$q$, 'draft')
