values ('141337b1-d5ab-5751-a1c2-4b5c0e030fa8', 'wg5-paragraph-transitions-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g5-paragraph-transitions'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Learning the Steel Pan$q$, $q$(1) This fall, our music class started learning to play the steel pan. (2) The steel pan is a drum that was first made on the island of Trinidad. (3) It is shaped like a large, shallow bowl, and its top is divided into many dented sections. (4) Each section plays a different note when you tap it with a rubber-tipped stick. (5) ____, the small sections near the center make high notes, while the larger ones near the edge make low notes.

(6) Learning to play was harder than I expected. (7) At first, I kept hitting the space between two notes. (8) ____, my songs sounded more like clanging pots than music. (9) My teacher, Mr. Baptiste, showed me how to keep my wrist loose and bounce the stick off the metal. (10) I practiced every day for two weeks. (11) My sister plays the clarinet in the middle school band. (12) By our winter concert, I could play a whole song without a single wrong note.$q$, 'draft')
