        '3-5', $q$How a 3D Printer Works$q$, $q$(1) A 3D printer can turn a computer drawing into a real object you can hold. (2) ____, a person designs the object on a computer. (3) Next, a program slices the design into hundreds of thin, flat layers. (4) The printer then heats a thin plastic string until it is soft. (5) A nozzle squeezes out the melted plastic, drawing the bottom layer first. (6) As each layer cools, it hardens and sticks to the one below it. (7) ____, the printer builds the whole object one layer at a time, from bottom to top.

