   $q$Read the paragraph: "(1) Recycling aluminum cans saves energy. (2) Making a can from old cans uses much less power than making one from new metal. (3) Old cans can also be melted down and turned into new cans again and again. (4) ____" Which sentence best concludes the paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"For these reasons, putting cans in the recycling bin is a smart choice.","is_correct":true},{"text":"First, rinse the cans before putting them in the bin.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-idea"},{"text":"Aluminum is a light, shiny kind of metal.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic"},{"text":"However, some people still throw cans in the trash.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-idea"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$For these reasons, putting cans in the recycling bin is a smart choice.$q$, $q$"For these reasons" pulls together the benefits in sentences 2 and 3 and restates the main idea. The sentence about people throwing cans away is tempting because it is about recycling, but it starts a new idea instead of wrapping up the paragraph.$q$, 'draft', null)
