   $q$Which sentence best fills blank (2) as the claim of the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Plastic is used to make bottles, toys, and many other things.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-claim"},{"text":"Osei shows that every new house should be built only from plastic.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-evidence"},{"text":"Osei shows that the bricks are made by melting plastic and sand.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Osei shows that plastic bricks are a good building material and a way to reduce plastic waste.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Osei shows that plastic bricks are a good building material and a way to reduce plastic waste.$q$, $q$Paragraph 1 is about the bricks as building material and paragraph 2 is about reducing waste, matching the "two problems" in sentence 12. The choice about melting plastic only describes how the bricks are made, so it is too narrow.$q$, 'draft', '8a5b0a8e-c0cf-50db-af33-f88b0742464f')
