-- Passage wg5-writing-with-evidence-p07
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('c7bb7079-9eaa-595b-bffb-6e5e1aa8ee39', 'wg5-writing-with-evidence-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g5-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Draft: The Toughest Tiny Animal$q$, $q$(1) In the article "The Toughest Tiny Animal," Farid Haddad describes tardigrades, which are animals smaller than a grain of sand. (2) ____.

(3) Haddad explains that tardigrades live in wet moss and damp leaves. (4) When their home dries out, they pull in their legs and curl into a dry ball. (5) He writes that a tardigrade can stay this way for many years. (6) When water returns, it uncurls and starts moving again within a few hours. (7) This shows that tardigrades can wait out a dry time instead of dying.

(8) Tardigrades can survive other hard conditions, too. (9) Haddad reports that scientists have found them living in freezing ice and in hot springs. (10) ____.

(11) My sister has a microscope, but it is broken. (12) In the end, Haddad shows that being small does not mean being weak.$q$, 'draft')
