insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('439deb21-3e57-54af-a458-ef1b71070df0', 'wg6-argument-writing-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-argument-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$A Weather Station for Cedar Grove$q$, $q$(1) Every morning, students at Cedar Grove Middle School check a phone app to learn whether it will rain. (2) Instead of relying only on apps, our school should build its own weather station. (3) A weather station would let students collect real data about temperature, rainfall, and wind speed right outside their classrooms. (4) Science classes could use those numbers to make graphs and test their predictions. (5) Working with real numbers makes science feel useful instead of distant.

(6) Some people may say that a weather station is too expensive for a school. (7) However, a basic station costs about as much as one classroom set of calculators. (8) ______ the parent group has already offered to raise half of the money at the spring fair.

(9) A weather station would turn our schoolyard into an outdoor science lab that every grade could use.$q$, 'draft')
