   $q$Read the sentence: "My cousin's band which practices in our garage played at the Harvest Fair on Saturday." Which revision is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"My cousin's band which practices in our garage, played at the Harvest Fair on Saturday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-opening-comma"},{"text":"My cousin's band which practices, in our garage, played at the Harvest Fair on Saturday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"commas-around-wrong-words"},{"text":"My cousin's band, which practices in our garage played at the Harvest Fair, on Saturday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-in-wrong-place"},{"text":"My cousin's band, which practices in our garage, played at the Harvest Fair on Saturday.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$My cousin's band, which practices in our garage, played at the Harvest Fair on Saturday.$q$, $q$A "which" clause that adds extra information is set off by commas at both ends, so the commas go before "which" and after "garage." Putting commas around only "in our garage" leaves "which practices" stuck to the subject.$q$, 'draft', null)
