   $q$Read the sentence: "Ines saw a monarch butterfly the kind that travels south each fall resting on the fence." Which revision correctly sets off the extra information?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Ines saw a monarch butterfly, the kind that travels south each fall resting on the fence.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-closing-comma"},{"text":"Ines saw a monarch butterfly the kind that travels, south each fall, resting on the fence.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"commas-around-wrong-words"},{"text":"Ines saw a monarch butterfly (the kind that travels south) each fall resting on the fence.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"parentheses-around-wrong-words"},{"text":"Ines saw a monarch butterfly (the kind that travels south each fall) resting on the fence.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Ines saw a monarch butterfly (the kind that travels south each fall) resting on the fence.$q$, $q$"The kind that travels south each fall" is an aside about the butterfly, so the whole phrase is enclosed in parentheses. The choice that puts a comma after "butterfly" opens the aside but never closes it, so "fall resting on the fence" runs together.$q$, 'draft', null)
