   $q$Read the sentence: "Dr. Achterberg a scientist who studies glaciers will speak to our class on Friday." Which revision is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Dr. Achterberg a scientist who studies glaciers, will speak to our class on Friday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-opening-comma"},{"text":"Dr. Achterberg, a scientist, who studies glaciers, will speak to our class on Friday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"appositive-split"},{"text":"Dr. Achterberg, a scientist who studies glaciers will speak to our class on Friday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-closing-comma"},{"text":"Dr. Achterberg, a scientist who studies glaciers, will speak to our class on Friday.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Dr. Achterberg, a scientist who studies glaciers, will speak to our class on Friday.$q$, $q$The whole phrase "a scientist who studies glaciers" renames Dr. Achterberg, so one comma goes before it and one after it. The choice "Dr. Achterberg, a scientist, who studies glaciers, will speak" adds a comma after "scientist," which wrongly splits the appositive from the clause that tells what kind of scientist Dr. Achterberg is.$q$, 'draft', null)
